#lang rmn/v2
(map
  ("type" "SoftwareProgramSynthesisLaw")
  ("version" 4)
  ("provider" "one sovereign software program circuit-layout settlement")
  ("precondition" "One signed A2A 1.0 Message carries exactly one canonical RMN/CBOR SoftwareProgramSynthesisSolicitation addressed to this settlement, naming the customer and one exact SoftwareProgramSynthesisRequest. Execution requires a second signed A2A Message carrying the provider's exact offer, that request, and an exact customer ResourceGrant covering the offered effects. The program names bounded territory, an explicit acceptance catalog, resource ceilings, and whether spatial write confinement is enforced.")
  ("operation" "Author an offer bound to the solicitation, request, program, this law, invocation operation, effects, requirements, and stable intent. Only after validating an exact customer contract and resource grant, place a supplied exact mission topology directly, including the one-bundle one-vertex case; purchase one typed plan only when topology is absent. Admit only an acyclic plan whose mission patches and acceptance gates cover the request, project its causal-spatial circuit, and obtain the configured independent hierarchical-circuit assay. Hire every causally ready and spatially nonconflicting software-mission settlement without a global execution-sheet barrier. Append a content-addressed witness journal invocation event before each hire. When it settles, require the signed A2A provider identity plus exact input and output ni receipt identities and append them in the causally dependent witness journal settlement event; that event alone releases its integrated causal successors while spacelike work may continue. A2A carries requests and receipts; RMN owns meaning; deterministic CBOR and RFC 6920 ni own identity.")
  ("postcondition" "The contracted result binds the customer, offer, contract, request, program, selected plan, exact causal-spatial circuit, distinct typed equivalence judgment with exact attribution and replay evidence, monotone mission-settlement events and their causal predecessors, mission provider receipts, typed economic measures, and final protected acceptance or unresolved residue. No solicitation becomes a filesystem queue item, no slow spacelike supplier delays an otherwise ready successor, and no provider writes a foreign interior.")
  ("refusal" "Refuse noncanonical bytes, an uncontracted or foreign request, a mismatched offer, insufficient resource grant, unknown acceptance gates, cyclic dependency, uncovered required patches, false spatial separation, absent mission provider receipts, customer-border overwrite, or resource escalation before executing the program.")
  ("invariants" ("one-layout-die" "provider-authored-offer-precedes-execution" "uncontracted-request-never-executes" "fully-specified-topology-is-placed-without-inference" "at-most-one-planning-contact" "no-filesystem-queue" "no-global-execution-sheet-barrier" "no-customer-package-import" "no-direct-json-semantic-path" "tensor-concurrency-requires-enforced-disjoint-custody" "causal-successors-release-from-exact-settlement-events" "mission-execution-is-a-hired-settlement" "par-is-not-manufactured-by-this-die")))
